Wabcut @WABCUT_VERSION@ - third-party notices
==============================================

Wabcut is free software, licensed under the GNU General Public License version 3 or later (LICENSE.txt).
This distribution contains or links the third-party components below. Their full license texts are in the
licenses/ directory next to this file. Versions are the ones this package was built with.

Qt @WABCUT_QT_VERSION@ (The Qt Company Ltd. and other contributors)
    License: GNU Lesser General Public License version 3 (licenses/qt-LGPL-3.0.txt, which supplements the
    GNU GPL version 3 in LICENSE.txt). Qt is linked dynamically; its libraries, plugins and QML modules are
    the separate files deployed by windeployqt/macdeployqt (Qt6*.dll, plugins, qml/). Qt sources:
    https://download.qt.io/official_releases/qt/
    Modules used: Qt Core, Gui, Quick, Quick Controls 2, Svg, Shader Tools; QRhi through Qt Gui private API.

FFmpeg @V_ffmpeg@ (the FFmpeg developers)
    License: @FFMPEG_LICENSE@ (licenses/ffmpeg.txt). This is a GPL build of FFmpeg.
    Libraries built: libavcodec, libavformat, libavfilter, libavutil, libswresample, libswscale (the runtime
    list at the end shows the ones this distribution ships).
    Source: https://ffmpeg.org/download.html (vcpkg port "ffmpeg").
    Configuration:
@FFMPEG_CONFIGURATION@

x264 @V_x264@ (VideoLAN)
    License: GNU General Public License version 2 or later (licenses/x264.txt). Linked by FFmpeg.

x265 @V_x265@ (MulticoreWare)
    License: GNU General Public License version 2 or later (licenses/x265.txt). Linked by FFmpeg.

dav1d @V_dav1d@ (VideoLAN and dav1d authors)
    License: BSD 2-Clause (licenses/dav1d.txt). AV1 decoder, linked by FFmpeg.

Intel VPL (libvpl) @V_libvpl@ (Intel Corporation)
    License: MIT (licenses/libvpl.txt). Quick Sync Video dispatcher, linked by FFmpeg.

SVT-AV1 @V_svt_av1@ (Alliance for Open Media, Intel Corporation, Netflix, Inc. and contributors)
    License: BSD 3-Clause Clear License, with the Alliance for Open Media Patent License 1.0 (both in
    licenses/svt-av1.txt). The AV1 software encoder (libSvtAv1Enc), linked by FFmpeg; AV1 exports use it when no
    hardware AV1 encoder (NVENC, Quick Sync, AMF) is present.

FAST corner detectors (fastfeat) @V_fastfeat@ (Edward Rosten)
    License: BSD 3-Clause (licenses/fastfeat.txt). Linked by SVT-AV1.

libvpx @V_libvpx@ (The WebM Project authors)
    License: BSD 3-Clause, with Google's additional IP rights grant (patents) and ISC parts (licenses/libvpx.txt).
    The VP9 encoder of WebM exports, linked by FFmpeg.

Opus @V_opus@ (Xiph.Org Foundation, Skype Limited, Octasic, Jean-Marc Valin, Timothy B. Terriberry, CSIRO, Gregory
Maxwell, Mark Borgerding, Erik de Castro Lopo, Mozilla, Amazon)
    License: BSD 3-Clause (licenses/opus.txt). The audio encoder of WebM exports, linked by FFmpeg.

AMD AMF headers @V_amd_amf@ and NVIDIA codec headers (nv-codec-headers) @V_ffnvcodec@
    Licenses: licenses/amd-amf.txt and licenses/ffnvcodec.txt (MIT). Header-only; the drivers are loaded at
    run time from the operating system and are not part of this distribution.

miniaudio @V_miniaudio@ (David Reid)
    License: public domain (Unlicense) or MIT No Attribution, at your choice (licenses/miniaudio.txt).
    Compiled into Wabcut.

libebur128 @V_libebur128@ (Jan Kokemüller)
    License: MIT (licenses/libebur128.txt). EBU R128 / ITU-R BS.1770 loudness measurement, compiled into Wabcut.

RNNoise @V_rnnoise@ (Jean-Marc Valin, Xiph.Org Foundation, Mozilla, Amazon)
    License: BSD 3-Clause (licenses/rnnoise.txt), including its trained model. The Reduce Noise audio effect,
    compiled into Wabcut.

JSON for Modern C++ (nlohmann_json) @V_nlohmann_json@ (Niels Lohmann)
    License: MIT (licenses/nlohmann-json.txt). Header-only, compiled into Wabcut.

pugixml @V_pugixml@ (Arseny Kapoulkine)
    License: MIT (licenses/pugixml.txt).

zlib @V_zlib@ (Jean-loup Gailly and Mark Adler)
    License: zlib License (licenses/zlib.txt).

spdlog @V_spdlog@ (Gabi Melman) and {fmt} @V_fmt@ (Victor Zverovich)
    Licenses: MIT (licenses/spdlog.txt, licenses/fmt.txt). Declared dependencies; included here when linked.

QtKeychain @V_qtkeychain@ (Frank Osterfeld and contributors)
    License: BSD 3-Clause (licenses/qtkeychain.txt). Keeps AI provider keys in the OS keychain; included in builds
    with WABCUT_WITH_CLOUD_AI (the default).

SQLite @V_sqlite3@ (D. Richard Hipp and the SQLite developers)
    License: public domain (the SQLite "blessing", licenses/sqlite3.txt). Smart search's index: transcript
    full-text search (FTS5, trigram tokenizer).

hnswlib @V_hnswlib@ (Yury Malkov, Leonid Boytsov and contributors)
    License: Apache License 2.0 (licenses/hnswlib.txt). Header-only; smart search's vector index.

CLAP @V_clap_cleveraudio@ (Alexandre Bique and the free-audio contributors) - builds with WABCUT_WITH_AUDIO_PLUGINS
    License: MIT (licenses/clap-cleveraudio.txt). The CLAP plugin ABI headers, compiled into the wabcut-plughost
    helper that hosts CLAP audio plugins.

VST 3 SDK @V_vst3sdk@ (Steinberg Media Technologies GmbH) - builds with WABCUT_WITH_AUDIO_PLUGINS
    License: MIT (licenses/vst3sdk.txt; Steinberg relicensed the SDK under MIT with version 3.8). Its interfaces and
    hosting classes are compiled into the wabcut-plughost helper that hosts VST3 audio plugins. VST is a registered
    trademark of Steinberg Media Technologies GmbH.

ONNX Runtime @V_onnxruntime_prebuilt@ (Microsoft Corporation) - builds with WABCUT_WITH_ONNX
    License: MIT (licenses/onnxruntime-prebuilt.txt, which includes Microsoft's notices for the code ONNX Runtime
    contains). Microsoft's official release binaries (onnxruntime.dll / libonnxruntime, unmodified), used by the
    wabcut-embed helper with its telemetry disabled. On Windows, DirectML comes from the operating system
    (System32\DirectML.dll) and is not part of this distribution.

whisper.cpp @V_whisper_cpp@ and ggml @V_ggml@ (the ggml authors) - builds with WABCUT_WITH_LOCAL_AI
    License: MIT (licenses/whisper-cpp.txt, licenses/ggml.txt; details in licenses/ai-local-helper.md). Local
    transcription in the wabcut-infer helper: whisper.dll, ggml.dll, ggml-base.dll and the compute backends ggml loads
    at run time (ggml-cpu-*.dll, one per CPU instruction-set level, and ggml-vulkan.dll).

Vulkan Loader @V_vulkan_loader@ (The Khronos Group Inc., Valve Corporation, LunarG, Inc.) - builds with
WABCUT_WITH_LOCAL_AI
    License: Apache License 2.0 (licenses/vulkan-loader.txt). vulkan-1.dll, loaded by ggml's Vulkan backend; the GPU
    drivers themselves come from the operating system.

llama.cpp llama-server, build b11429 (the ggml authors) - downloaded on request, not part of this distribution
    License: MIT. The local assistant (Preferences > AI > Local assistant) downloads the official release archives
    from https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/releases/tag/b11429 only when you press Download, and verifies them
    by SHA-256. Its model weights (Qwen3, Apache License 2.0; Phi-4 mini, MIT) are downloaded the same way
    after their license cards are shown. The optional NVIDIA CUDA runtime archive is under the NVIDIA CUDA Toolkit
    EULA and is never downloaded without your explicit acceptance.

SigLIP 2 base, patch 16, 224 px (Google) - downloaded on first use, not part of this distribution
    License: Apache License 2.0, with its Gemma tokenizer vocabulary; ONNX export and 8-bit quantization by
    onnx-community. Smart search downloads it from Hugging Face into the model store (verified by SHA-256) after
    showing its license: https://huggingface.co/google/siglip2-base-patch16-224

YuNet face detector, face_detection_yunet_2023mar (Shiqi Yu, OpenCV Model Zoo) - downloaded on first use, not part of
this distribution
    License: MIT (Copyright (c) 2020 Shiqi Yu). Auto reframe and the shorts finder run it in wabcut-embed on this
    computer; downloaded from Hugging Face (opencv/face_detection_yunet, pinned revision) into the model store,
    verified by SHA-256, after showing its license: https://github.com/opencv/opencv_zoo/tree/main/models/face_detection_yunet

YOLOX-Tiny object detector, release 0.1.1rc0 (Megvii Inc.) - downloaded on first use, not part of this distribution
    License: Apache License 2.0 (Copyright (c) 2021-2022 Megvii Inc.), trained on COCO. Auto reframe uses its person
    class, the AI Object Mask its 80 classes, in wabcut-embed on this computer; downloaded from the release's GitHub assets into the model store, verified
    by SHA-256, after showing its license: https://github.com/Megvii-BaseDetection/YOLOX

DeepFilterNet3 (Hendrik Schroeter) - downloaded on first use, not part of this distribution
    License: MIT OR Apache-2.0 for the code and the weights, used under MIT (Copyright (c) 2021 Hendrik Schroeter).
    Enhance Speech runs it in wabcut-embed on this computer; the ONNX archive of the repository at commit 84d57ec is
    downloaded into the model store, verified by SHA-256 (archive and each graph), after showing its license:
    https://github.com/Rikorose/DeepFilterNet
    Wabcut's DeepFilterNet signal processing (src/ai/audio/src/DeepFilter.cpp) is a port of libDF from that
    repository, under the same MIT License and copyright (THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md has the license text).

HTDemucs (Simon Rouard, Francisco Massa, Alexandre Defossez; Meta) - downloaded on first use, not part of this
distribution
    License: MIT (Copyright (c) Meta Platforms, Inc. and affiliates), the weights as released with Demucs v4; ONNX
    export by StemSplit, MIT (Copyright (c) 2026 StemSplit). Separate Stems runs it in wabcut-embed on this computer;
    downloaded from Hugging Face (StemSplitio/htdemucs-onnx, pinned revision) into the model store, verified by
    SHA-256, after showing its license: https://github.com/facebookresearch/demucs

OPUS-MT caption translation models (Joerg Tiedemann, Santhosh Thottingal; Language Technology Research Group,
University of Helsinki) - downloaded on first use, not part of this distribution
    License: Apache License 2.0, except opus-mt-en-de and opus-mt-zh-en under Creative Commons Attribution 4.0
    (c) Language Technology Research Group, University of Helsinki, https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/;
    converted to ONNX and 8-bit quantized by Xenova, otherwise unmodified. Captions are translated in wabcut-embed on
    this computer; each pair's files are downloaded from Hugging Face (Xenova/opus-mt-<pair>, pinned revisions) into the
    model store, verified by SHA-256, after showing the model card: https://github.com/Helsinki-NLP/Opus-MT
    Pairs: en-mul, th-en, en-es, en-fr, en-de, en-zh, ja-en, ko-en, zh-en, es-en, fr-en, de-en

SAM 2.1 Hiera-Tiny (Segment Anything Model 2.1; Nikhila Ravi et al., Meta FAIR) - downloaded on first use, not part
of this distribution
    License: Apache License 2.0 (Copyright (c) Meta Platforms, Inc. and affiliates), the code and the model weights
    (facebook/sam2.1-hiera-tiny); ONNX export of its video tracker by square-zero-labs, Apache License 2.0, revision
    3b2984dd865f6e9d2cc6aed0be6a5a5c2eb352ce. The AI Object Mask runs it in wabcut-embed on this computer; downloaded
    from Hugging Face (square-zero-labs/sam2.1-tiny-video-onnx, pinned revision) into the model store, every file
    verified by SHA-256, after showing its license: https://github.com/facebookresearch/sam2

Boxicons 3 (@boxicons/core 1.0.6, Copyright (c) 2026 Boxicons)
    License: MIT (licenses/boxicons.txt). The icon set used by the user interface. The monitor-button glyphs, the
    drag grip and text glyphs, the logo and the empty-state illustrations are Wabcut's own drawings.

Manrope 4.504 (Copyright 2019 The Manrope Project Authors)
    License: SIL Open Font License 1.1 (licenses/OFL-Manrope.txt). The user-interface and display font, bundled in
    the application's resources.

JetBrains Mono 2.304 (Copyright 2020 The JetBrains Mono Project Authors)
    License: SIL Open Font License 1.1 (licenses/OFL-JetBrains-Mono.txt). The timecode and numbers font, bundled in
    the application's resources.

IBM Plex Sans 1.1.0, IBM Plex Sans Thai 1.1.0 and IBM Plex Mono 2.5.0 (Copyright 2017 IBM Corp., Reserved Font
Name "Plex")
    License: SIL Open Font License 1.1 (licenses/OFL-IBM-Plex.txt). The Thai user-interface font, and fonts for
    titles and captions, bundled in the application's resources.

Bai Jamjuree 1.000 (Copyright 2018 Cadson Demak)
    License: SIL Open Font License 1.1 (licenses/OFL-Bai-Jamjuree.txt). A font for titles and captions, bundled in
    the application's resources.


Catch2 @V_catch2@ (Catch2 authors) - test only
    License: Boost Software License 1.0 (licenses/catch2.txt). Used by the test suites only; not part of the
    Wabcut executables.

Microsoft runtime files (Windows only)
    The Visual C++ runtime (vcruntime140*.dll, msvcp140*.dll, concrt140.dll), the D3D shader compiler
    (d3dcompiler_47.dll) and the DirectX Shader Compiler (dxcompiler.dll, dxil.dll, used by Qt's Direct3D 12
    backend) are redistributable files of Microsoft Visual Studio and the Windows SDK, distributed under
    Microsoft's license terms for those products.

Corresponding source for the GPL components, and for Wabcut itself, is available from the Wabcut source
repository together with the vcpkg manifest (vcpkg.json) and baseline that pin every version above.
